1. What is MDC?
MDC allows us to attach contextual information to logs.
For example, imagine multiple requests hitting your Spring Boot application:
Request 1 → Customer ID: 101
Request 2 → Customer ID: 205
Request 3 → Customer ID: 301
Normally, logs may look like:
10:10:01 INFO  Getting customer
10:10:01 INFO  Getting account
10:10:02 ERROR Customer not found
It can be difficult to identify which request produced which log.
With MDC:
10:10:01 [requestId=abc123] INFO  Getting customer
10:10:01 [requestId=abc123] INFO  Getting account

10:10:02 [requestId=xyz789] ERROR Customer not found
Now we can easily track all logs belonging to a particular request.
In simple words
MDC stores contextual data for the current thread so that the information can automatically appear in every log generated during that request.


